      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hmmm I suppose wanting to look out for new users is a good thing. But are you referring to actual events, or public instances?\nBecause if it's an event, I'd assume whoever created the instance would be able to moderate it. Why block someone when you should have kicked them instead.\nIf someone does it repeatedly, then.. Yeah, it's an issue. I'd say it's VRChat's job to moderate such users, but that obviously won't always be possible in a timely manner.\nI'm not sure a badge is the best solution for this. Actual moderation tools would be wonderful. https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/moderation-tools-for-world-creators",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
