      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f8a26770aaa28611fedd6b6|full_name}: The reason I block certain users is to determine if they are annoying users or not.\nCurrently, there are several methods for marking annoying users, such as \"Block\", \"Mute\", and \"Hide Avatar\".\nOf these, \"Hide Avatar\" can only be controlled by actually being in the same instance as the player in VRChat.\n\"Block\" and \"Mute\" can be done from vrchat.com, but if you do this, you will not be able to see their actions (e.g. insults, harassment).\nHowever, if these features can be implemented optionally by users through Udon, this will be solved.\nThank you for a meaningful discussion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
